  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Mozambique Country Programme works to reduce the time, cost, and complexity of trade along the Beira Corridor, a critical transit route linking landlocked Malawi and Zimbabwe to the Port of Beira and onward to regional and global markets. Operating since 2020, the Programme targets three interconnected priorities: improving corridor and border efficiency at key nodes including Beira Port and the Machipanda border crossing through trade facilitation measures and digital customs systems developed in partnership with the Mozambique Revenue Authority; strengthening agricultural export competitiveness by digitising phytosanitary certification through the e-Phyto system, which has reduced certificate processing times from an average of twelve days to two to three, and building private sector and institutional capacity to meet sanitary and phytosanitary standards for value chains such as mango; and promoting inclusive trade with targeted support for women traders at Machipanda, improving their access to trade information, financial services, and formalisation pathways.</narrative>
  </description>
